    "diagnosis": "Molecular classifications of breast cancer with prognostic relevance",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Clinical subtypes of breast cancer based on their receptor profiles (ER and ERBB2 [HER2]) have imperfect overlap with the intrinsic molecular subtypes. Triple-negative breast cancers are further defined into additional molecular subtypes. Integrative cluster subtypes based on more-comprehensive genomic profiling further risk stratify the clinical and intrinsic molecular subtypes; however, they are not currently available clinically. Clinically, prognostic signatures such as the 21-gene recurrence score can further stratify risk in the favourable prognosis ER+/HER2&minus; subtype.",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Salgado R,&nbsp;Sotiriou C",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/84/45/",
